 "_doc": "earshot's listening vocabulary: short caption-like phrases CLAP scores sounds against. 'templates' are prompt ensembles (each term is embedded through every template and averaged). Every term in every category also forms the background distribution used to calibrate scores (z = how far a match stands out from what an arbitrary description would score). History (for honest validation): 217 terms were written before any evaluation (eval/semantics/vocab_preregistered.json); 67 were added after seeing the 219-file tuning library's classes (tuned to it); 38 general everyday terms (vehicles, household, tools, animals, people) were added from general knowledge; the list was then frozen before the held-out library (eval/semantics/heldout_labels.json) was scored. Extending it changes every z a little: re-run eval/semantics/run_eval.py analyze + heldout afterwards. data/vocab_stats.json holds the reference mean embedding (independent of the vocabulary) and a derived table of each term's mean / std cosine over the reference recordings.",
